+## Hand-drawn input
+
+Scenes drawn with one black marker and photographed ([DESIGN_SKETCH.md](DESIGN_SKETCH.md)).
+Training data is generated by `sim/sketch.py` (`generate.py --style sketch`):
+every primitive is perturbed once and the same perturbed geometry is drawn into
+the image and the label map, and the scene JSON records what was *drawn*, so
+labels and instance targets stay exact. The real test set is traced on printed
+sheets and needs no annotation either.
+
+```bash
+python scripts/make_datasets.py --only "*sketch*" --jobs 3       # train_sketch, val_sketch, test_sketch
+python train.py --data-root data --train train_sketch train_aug3 --val val_sketch \
+                --size 256 --instance-head --wall-mode lines --seed 0 --out runs/sketch_s256_inst_s0
+python scripts/make_sheets.py                                    # print reference.pdf + drawing.pdf at 100 %
+# trace each scene, photograph each drawing sheet with all four corner squares in view, then
+python scripts/ingest_photos.py path/to/photos                   # -> data/real_sketch/test/
+python evaluate.py --ckpt runs/sketch_s256_inst_s0/ckpt_best.pt \
+                   --data data/test data/test_aug3 data/test_sketch data/real_sketch/test
+python predict.py --ckpt runs/sketch_s256_inst_s0/ckpt_best.pt --image IMG_0042.jpg --photo --out parsed/
+```
+
+- **Output like a generated scene.** With `--wall-mode lines` (`walllines.py`)
+  walls come back as a few straight, axis-parallel centre lines with the
+  generator's 3-unit thickness, however wobbly the pen was; obstacles are
+  circle fits and regions boxes in either mode. `predict.py` then also writes
+  `<name>_clean.png`, the parse re-drawn by the generator's own renderer, and
+  the JSON's `world.wall_thickness` is 3.0 — build the simulator with
+  `extract.sim_config(cfg, parsed)`. The default `surface` mode is the E5
+  behaviour.
+
+- `--train` takes several directories; they are concatenated and the class
+  weights come from their combined pixel counts. A single `--train` is stored
+  as a string, as before.
+- `ingest_photos.py` prints every rejected photo with its reason (usually a
+  corner square outside the photo: retake it). The first photo of a sheet wins.
+- On `real_sketch/test` the label PNGs are rendered from the JSON only so the
+  loader works; `evaluate.py` reports its pixel metrics and wall surface error
+  as NaN. Agent, obstacle, region and `scene_usable` metrics are real.
+- Look at a few generated scenes before a long run:
+  `python ../sim/generate.py --n 7 --style sketch --preview 7 --out data/preview_sketch`.
+
